 lines+=['','All matchups use fresh seeds11101011+i*1009, both sides, same real2second forecast schema for both actors, greedy mode/tanh steering, complete300active-second regulation.120second overtime and900second total caps are censored, not draws. Full metrics and engine-contact recovery lists are in records.json/result.json. Circling, velocity-direction contact quality and missed approaches are explicitly proxies. A near pass without touch is not necessarily a feasible missed interception. Car-contact cooldown refreshes detect engine contact; recovery is reaching400UU/s grounded, not tactical success. Unresolved/censored events remain visible.','', '## What changed and what did not','', 'Actor initialized ONLY from Outcome128. Ground64 previously learned forecast dependence (mean ablation steering change~0.0279) but failed competitive qualification, including1W9L2U vsGeometric in previous fresh screen. Its actor was used only as a frozen legal opponent here. This experiment enabled actual forecasts and gradients into formerly zero forecast encoder columns. No direct-ball pursuit targets, mode cross-entropy, teacher labels, auxiliary prediction heads, runtime manoeuvres or new parameters. Four fresh PPO epochs, joint categorical/tanh-Normal behavior probabilities, small joint reference-policy KL(.02), unchanged reward coefficients, all twelve chronological2048-step sequences from reset; hidden memory carried over goals. Twelve trajectories include normal, attack, defence, allfive kickoffs and recovery. Frozen pool: Outcome, Ground, Geometric, OriginalV13; each occurs3times. Training scenario/opponent/side assignment is not a fully crossed design; match evaluation is side-paired.','', 'Original observation-only critic and Adam were reused as training-only value state; rejected PPO actor weights were never loaded. Earlier memory-critic diagnostic had rejected the change. Actor uses fresh PPO Adam because initialization came from a supervised objective; original supervised optimizer/checkpoints remain preserved. Value bootstrap is retained at nonterminal rollout cutoff; reset potential correction accounts for goal resets. Forecasts are regenerated by realRocketSim241samples at120Hz, indexed at2seconds; future car interventions are not known. No native prediction packets invented.','',f"Every rollout had forecast valid=1; actual callback delta first0 then1 at60Hz. Forecast gradient norms {v['forecast_gradient_norms']}; final forecast column norms {v['forecast_input_column_norms']}. Recurrent replay, collected log probabilities, save/reload equality, whole-vs-chunk sequence parity and26181parameter/8tensor checks passed. Forecast first-slice offset is constant0 in this simulator data; native offset variation and missing forecasts were not trained in this batch.",'',f"Training-trajectory forecast ablation: mean absolute steering change across trajectories {np.mean([r['forecast_ablation_steer_mean'] for r in v['rows']]):.6f}; mode changes {sum(r['forecast_ablation_mode_changes'] for r in v['rows'])}/24576. This is weak learned forecast sensitivity, not demonstrated anticipation or better gameplay.",'','## Reward and learning signal audit','',f"Unchanged goals+10/-10, potential-based goal progress/car-ball distance, .08 clipped signed ball delta-velocity at qualified contacts, -.003 nonproductive contacts and -.001 per60Hz step sustained stationary penalty. Each component saved perdecision; sums {v['reward_component_sums']} in order goal/potential/productive_velocity/nonproductive_contact/stationary/reset_potential. {sum(g['goal_for'] for r in roll for g in r['goals'])} goals scored and {sum(not g['goal_for'] for r in roll for g in r['goals'])} conceded; {sum(r['contacts']['touch'] for r in roll)} own contact callbacks. Netzero goal reward does not mean no goal events.",f"Sampled modes {np.array([r['sampled_modes'] for r in v['rows']]).sum(0).tolist()} versus deterministic replay {np.array([r['greedy_modes'] for r in v['rows']]).sum(0).tolist()} (Neutral,Chase,Jump,Dodge). Thus35.0% sampledJump/Dodge, while tournament-like greedy behavior remainsChase. This distribution mismatch plus sparse useful contacts is a plausible weak-learning-signal issue, not a proven sole cause. No extra experiment was launched to tune it.",f"{sum(r['abrupt_ball_velocity_changes'] for r in roll)} abrupt ball velocity changes>300UU/s and{sum(r['opponent_touch_callbacks'] for r in roll)} opponent-touch callbacks expose reaction states. No evidence establishes improved challenge anticipation. Rewards unchanged; no isolated causal reward ablation was run, so no claim that goal-direction rewards caused improvement.",'','## Observation limits','', 'The actor sees only local current/predicted ball positions, distance, speed, availability and timing. It has no opponent position or field/goal-relative heading. A180degree rotation of car, ball and their histories while keeping the team fixed can preserve these local observations but reverse which global goal should be attacked. Therefore reliable own-goal/enemy-goal identification is not generally possible under the contract, even with recurrent history. History can detect ball-trajectory changes, not directly track opponents or uniquely identify who caused them. True global coordinates/team signs remain solely in reward and evaluation code.','', '## Integrity, Windows and submission','',f"Research checkpoint SHA256 {t['candidate_SHA256']}. Preserve all four optimizer checkpoints, latest state, input rollouts, RNG and code. Failed/unqualified experiment states are research backups, not recommended playing archives. Main remains c151310b5c36996aeb1fe192be5eea7cc328e846; all{v['all_prior_checkpoints_unchanged']} prior checkpoint hashes preserved. Official policy, observation contract, validator and workflow files remain byte-identical.",'', 'Windows recommendation remains Outcome128, with Geometric as the previously qualitatively tested reference; Ground64 stays diagnostic. Existing private Final-Candidate-Review-Windows package remains usable. In Outcome-128-reference run SETUP.cmd then CHECK.cmd, add its bot.toml in RLBotv5, run standard1v1 bothBlue/Orange against Original-V13 and Geometric-preferred; record complete scores and native errors. Folder names are historical; Outcome is this report\'s recommendation. No actualRocketLeague execution or Windows acceptance occurred in cloud.','', 'No merge/main replacement, organizer access, public sharing or submission is authorized. Official local validator results and SDK preflight are distinct from GitHubActions and native gameplay. New branch Actions not claimed passed. Deadline07:00IST; final user approval remains mandatory even if the deadline passes.']
